    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"Addressable through revisions\" sounds a bit optimistic to me, especially with Reviewer 3's note on the control group delta. If I look closer at the raw data in Section 4.2 of the manuscript, it looks like they used a non-parametric test on data that clearly violates the normality assumption, which basically invalidates their entire p-value calculation for the primary finding. \n\nIf that's the case here, a \"revision\" might just be a cosmetic fix for a broken foundation. Do you really think this is just a matter of refining the stats, or are we looking at a fundamental methodological failure that would make the paper's conclusions unreliable? I'm worried about the optics if we publish this and it gets torn apart later.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
